  "articleBody": "Trying to decide whether to simply repair something in your home or go for a full refresh? It's a common dilemma, and knowing the difference can save you a lot of headache and money. A 'repair' typically means fixing a broken or malfunctioning component to restore its original function. Think patching a leaky roof, replacing a cracked tile, or mending a broken fence. These are generally smaller, targeted fixes aimed at stopping further damage or bringing something back to working order. A 'refresh,' on the other hand, is about updating the aesthetics and feel of a space, often involving more extensive work like new paint, updated fixtures, or even minor layout changes to improve functionality and appearance. For example, you might repair a leaky faucet, but refresh your entire bathroom with new tiling and a vanity. The HH Remodeling LLC team, serving the greater Denver area including Centennial and Highlands Ranch, is adept at both. We can assess your situation – whether it's a small handyman job or a more comprehensive remodel – and help you weigh the costs and benefits of each approach. Sometimes a refresh can prevent future repairs, and sometimes a simple repair is all you truly need. Our goal is to make your house feel more like a home, whatever that takes.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-17"
